From b6598b9e976d13f2ab0aaf9324eeb051765f90f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:34:48 +1000
Subject: [PATCH v2 1/4] ui/spice: track a bounded list of damage rectangles

The simple spice display keeps the damage reported between two updates
as a single QXLRect, the union of everything reported. Two small,
distant changes, such as a video and a clock in opposite corners of
the screen, therefore become one rectangle spanning most of the
screen, and everything inside it gets diffed and, in part, resent.

Track up to SIMPLE_SPICE_DAMAGE_MAX_RECTS (16) rectangles instead.
A new rectangle that overlaps or touches existing damage is merged
with it into their bounding box, so the list stays disjoint; when the
list is full, the new rectangle is merged with the entry whose
bounding box grows the least.

The list lives in a small helper, ui/spice-damage.c, that does not
depend on spice or pixman, so that it can be unit tested on its own.
The column diff that turns damage into QXL draws is unchanged, it now
just runs once per rectangle.

Prompt: Harden the spice damage prototype toward upstream: make the
damage list logic unit testable under meson test, keep each patch
checkpatch clean and bisectable, and write qemu style commit messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
